# Gitignored files Claude Code copies into worktrees it creates.
# A file is copied only if it matches a pattern here AND is gitignored.

# The knowledge graph. Copying it is ~0s and makes a worktree usable
# immediately; building one costs ~45s. Note that copy-then-rebuild saves
# nothing — `graphify update` re-extracts ~1160 of 1486 files even when the
# graph is already current — so the graph is validated, never refreshed:
# graph.json records `built_at_commit`, and the SessionStart hook in
# .claude/settings.json compares it against the checkout's HEAD and retires
# the graph if they differ. Dated backup directories (graphify-out/<date>/,
# ~18 MB) are deliberately not listed.
graphify-out/graph.json
graphify-out/manifest.json
graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md
graphify-out/.graphify_labels.json
graphify-out/.graphify_labels.json.sig
graphify-out/.graphify_root
graphify-out/cache/**

# Prebuilt C helper. Rebuilding needs libgpod headers + make, and
# @podkit/gpod-testing shells out to it, so test:unit needs it present.
bin/gpod-tool
